---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = "About Wa-Node (Profile & Business Overview) | LINE Integration Specialist";
const description = "Profile of Hirozumi Takano, founder of Wa-Node. Drawing on more than 20 years in IT, Wa-Node specialises in connecting LINE Official Accounts with Salesforce, kintone, HubSpot and Google Sheets for businesses.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} lang="en">
  <main id="main">
    <section class="section about-hero">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <span class="eyebrow">Profile</span>
        <h1>About Wa-Node</h1>
        <p class="lead">Wa-Node connects your LINE Official Account with Salesforce, kintone, HubSpot or Google Sheets,<br class="pc-only" />so inquiries reach your business system without manual copying.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section message">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <div class="message-content reveal">
          <div class="content-left">
            <h2>Founder's Message</h2>
            <h3 class="catch-copy">"When systems are not connected,<br class="sp-only"/>people keep doing the copying."</h3>
            <p>Since 2004 I have worked in IT for more than 20 years, from POS system maintenance and server operations to in-house systems, workflow automation and data management for web services. One situation came up again and again: <strong>"The systems are in place, yet people still sit between them, copying and pasting."</strong></p>
            <p>Living as a wheelchair user has taught me that inconvenience can be solved with ingenuity. The manual wall between LINE and your business system disappears when the integration is designed properly. That conviction is why I specialise in LINE integration.</p>
            <p>Wa-Node is a B2B partner specialising in connecting LINE with business systems (Salesforce, kintone, HubSpot and Google Sheets). Together with the people who already run those systems, we design a setup that frees them from manual work.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="content-right">
            <div class="profile-image-wrap">
              <img src="/images/avatar.webp" alt="Wa-Node founder Hirozumi Takano" />
              <p class="name-jp">高野 紘純</p>
              <p class="name-en">Hirozumi Takano</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section profile-details">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <div class="section-title">
          <span class="eyebrow">Profile & Skills</span>
          <h2>A partner specialising in LINE integration</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="story-box reveal">
          <h3>Why focus on LINE integration</h3>
          <p>Working in IT, I kept seeing people re-typing information even after a system was introduced: LINE inquiries copied by hand into customer management, or LINE applications tracked separately from everything else. The more systems there are, the more manual work there is.</p>
          <p>A LINE Official Account is a powerful point of contact, but it rarely works on its own. Only when LINE and your business system are properly connected do automated responses, a single source of customer data and fewer missed inquiries become possible.</p>
          <p>By focusing on LINE integration, Wa-Node takes responsibility from requirements through launch and maintenance.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="career-box">
          <h3>Career</h3>
          <ol class="career-list">
            <li><span class="career-year">1999–2004</span><p>Restaurant manager and franchise store management, including staff management. Certified as an Industrial Counselor in 2002.</p></li>
            <li><span class="career-year">2004</span><p>UNIX server monitoring and system operations at a manufacturing site.</p></li>
            <li><span class="career-year">2004–2008</span><p>Maintenance and repair of POS systems for restaurants (MS-DOS / Windows XP) and in-store LAN cabling.</p></li>
            <li><span class="career-year">2008–2010</span><p>In-house IT and process improvement at a reuse retail company. Built custom mobile terminals from compact PCs and remote-control software, roughly halving on-site working time. Also consolidated sales data in Access and installed and maintained servers.</p></li>
            <li><span class="career-year">2010–2024</span><p>Independent web and system projects.</p></li>
            <li><span class="career-year">2024–2025</span><p>Operated a data management system built on Bubble and Google Sheets, and ran a WordPress media site, at an IT and web services company.</p></li>
            <li><span class="career-year">2026</span><p>Founded Wa-Node, specialising in connecting LINE with business systems.</p></li>
          </ol>
        </div>

        <div class="qual-grid reveal">
          <div class="qual-item highlight-border">
            <h4>LINE Integration</h4>
            <ul>
              <li>LINE Messaging API / LIFF (web apps inside LINE)</li>
              <li>Salesforce REST API (leads, cases, accounts)</li>
              <li>kintone REST API (apps and records)</li>
              <li>HubSpot API (contacts and deals)</li>
              <li>Google Sheets integration (Apps Script)</li>
              <li>Webhook design and server-side implementation (Node.js, etc.)</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="qual-item">
            <h4>IT Engineering</h4>
            <ul>
              <li>More than 20 years in IT (since 2004)</li>
              <li>HTML5 / CSS3 / JavaScript (React, Astro)</li>
              <li>Fundamental Information Technology Engineer / Information Security Administrator (Japanese national IT examinations)</li>
              <li>Cisco certifications (CCNA, etc., obtained 2007) / Network design</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="qual-item">
            <h4>Requirements & Workflow Design</h4>
            <ul>
              <li>Interviews with IT staff and workflow mapping</li>
              <li>Record matching and data integration schema design</li>
              <li>Maintenance and changes after launch</li>
              <li>Industrial Counselor (since 2002) / Conversation design</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="qual-item">
            <h4>Lived Perspective & Numbers</h4>
            <ul>
              <li>Motivated as a wheelchair user to solve inconvenience with technology</li>
              <li>Barrier-Free Residential Environment Advisor</li>
              <li>Bookkeeping Grade 2 / Proposals grounded in cost-effectiveness</li>
              <li>Support after launch for small B2B teams</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section business-overview">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <div class="section-title">
          <span class="eyebrow">Overview</span>
          <h2>Business Overview</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="overview-table-wrap reveal">
          <table class="overview-table">
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <th>Business Name</th>
                <td>和-Node (Wa-Node)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th>Representative</th>
                <td>Hirozumi Takano</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th>Location</th>
                <td>2347-1 Imawatari, Kani City, Gifu, 509-0207, Japan</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th>Contact</th>
                <td><a href="mailto:contacts@wa-node.com">contacts@wa-node.com</a></td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th>Services</th>
                <td>
                  <ul>
                    <li><strong>LINE × Salesforce integration</strong>: from ¥400,000 (excl. tax)</li>
                    <li><strong>LINE × kintone integration</strong>: from ¥250,000 (excl. tax)</li>
                    <li><strong>LINE × HubSpot integration</strong>: from ¥200,000 (excl. tax)</li>
                    <li><strong>LINE × Google Sheets integration</strong>: from ¥100,000 (excl. tax)</li>
                    <li><strong>Maintenance and changes</strong>: ongoing support after launch</li>
                  </ul>
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th>Service Areas</th>
                <td>Nationwide in Japan (fully online), in person around Gifu and Aichi</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section reliability">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <div class="reliability-box reveal">
          <h2>Foundation of Trust & Security</h2>
          <div class="trust-grid">
            <div class="trust-item">
              <img src="/images/security-action-one-star.webp" alt="SECURITY ACTION Badge" class="trust-badge" />
              <p>We have declared our commitment to information security measures.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="trust-content">
              <ul>
                <li><strong>Integration quality</strong>: We take responsibility from requirements through launch and maintenance.</li>
                <li><strong>Information management</strong>: API keys, customer data and other confidential information are strictly managed to prevent leaks.</li>
                <li><strong>Transparent pricing</strong>: No unexpected charges or opaque billing without a prior quote.</li>
              </ul>
              <div class="policy-links">
                <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy (Japanese)</a>
                <a href="/security-policy/">Information Security Policy (Japanese)</a>
                <a href="/terms/">Terms of Service (Japanese)</a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section contact-teaser">
      <div class="section-inner text-center">
        <h2 class="reveal">Start by mapping your LINE and business system setup.</h2>
        <p class="reveal">In the free first consultation (30 min), we review your current LINE and system setup and what you want to connect.<br />An early idea is enough.</p>
        <div class="btns reveal" style="justify-content: center;">
          <a href="/en/contact/" class="btn primary">Discuss your LINE integration</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-hero {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #fdfcf9 0%, #f7f1e6 100%);
    text-align: center;
    padding: 120px 0 80px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .about-hero h1 { font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem); margin-bottom: 24px; color: var(--text-deep); }
  
  .message-content {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 1fr;
    gap: 60px;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .catch-copy {
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.2rem);
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-bottom: 24px;
    font-family: 'Shippori Mincho', serif;
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }
  .message-content p { margin-bottom: 20px; color: #444; font-size: 1.05rem; }
  
  .profile-image-wrap {
    text-align: center;
    background: #fff;
    padding: 40px;
    border-radius: 40px;
    box-shadow: 0 20px 40px rgba(0,0,0,0.05);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .profile-image-wrap img {
    width: 220px;
    height: 220px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    object-fit: cover;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
    background: var(--soft);
  }
  .name-jp { font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 800; margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .name-en { font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--accent); font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em; }

  .story-box {
    background: var(--soft);
    padding: 48px;
    border-radius: 24px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }
  .story-box h3 { margin-bottom: 24px; color: var(--accent); font-weight: 800; }
  .story-box p { margin-bottom: 16px; color: #444; line-height: 1.8; }

  .qual-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 32px;
  }
  .qual-item {
    background: #fff;
    padding: 40px;
    border-radius: 24px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .qual-item.highlight-border { border: 2px solid var(--accent); }
  .career-box { margin: 0 0 48px; padding: 36px 40px; background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px; }
  .career-box h3 { margin-bottom: 20px; color: var(--accent); font-weight: 800; }
  .career-list { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  .career-list li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 8.5em 1fr; gap: 16px; padding: 14px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .career-list li p { margin: 0; line-height: 1.8; }
  .career-year { font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent); white-space: nowrap; }
  @media (max-width: 560px) { .career-box { padding: 24px 20px; } .career-list li { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 4px; } }
  .qual-item h4 { margin-bottom: 20px; color: var(--accent); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); padding-bottom: 10px; font-weight: 800; }
  .qual-item ul { list-style: none; padding: 0; }
  .qual-item li { position: relative; padding-left: 20px; margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 0.95rem; color: #555; }
  .qual-item li::before { content: "•"; position: absolute; left: 0; color: var(--accent); font-weight: 800; }

  .overview-table-wrap {
    background: #fff;
    border-radius: 24px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .overview-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    text-align: left;
  }
  .overview-table th, .overview-table td {
    padding: 24px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .overview-table th {
    background: var(--soft);
    width: 250px;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--accent);
    vertical-align: top;
  }
  .overview-table td ul { padding-left: 20px; list-style: none; padding: 0; }
  .overview-table td li { margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .overview-table td li strong { color: var(--accent-dark); }
  .overview-table tr:last-child th, .overview-table tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }

  .reliability-box {
    background: var(--text-deep);
    color: #fff;
    padding: 80px 60px;
    border-radius: 40px;
  }
  .reliability-box h2 { color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 40px; font-weight: 800; }
  .trust-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 2fr; gap: 48px; align-items: center; }
  .trust-badge { width: 150px; background: #fff; border-radius: 12px; padding: 10px; }
  .trust-content ul { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin-bottom: 32px; }
  .trust-content li { margin-bottom: 16px; font-size: 0.95rem; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.8); }
  .trust-content strong { color: var(--accent); }
  
  .policy-links { display: flex; gap: 24px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .policy-links a { color: #fff; text-decoration: underline; font-size: 0.9rem; opacity: 0.7; transition: 0.3s; }
  .policy-links a:hover { opacity: 1; color: var(--accent); }

  .text-center { text-align: center; }

  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .message-content, .trust-grid, .qual-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .content-right { order: -1; }
    .profile-image-wrap img { width: 160px; height: 160px; }
    .overview-table th { width: 120px; font-size: 0.9rem; padding: 15px; }
    .overview-table td { padding: 15px; font-size: 0.9rem; }
    .reliability-box { padding: 40px 20px; }
  }
</style>
